title: Hamiltonian Path
text: V = {a, b, c, d, e, f, g}, top to bottom. E = {ab, ac, ad, ag, bc, bd, be, bf, cd, df}. No return ticket required.
trick: an arc diagram: each arc is one edge, a lane leaving one vertex row and joining another, and needs two reflectors. A beam crosses a vertex straight on, so it arrives on one side and leaves on the other; the toolbox holds exactly enough for a path through all seven vertices
motif: arc diagram: the vertices in a line down the middle, every edge a clear lane on one side, lanes crossing on occupied squares
expect: depth>=12
---
